<title>GERMANY: Waigel omits reference to trade tax in speech.</title>
<headline>Waigel omits reference to trade tax in speech.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel omitted a reference to trade tax on capital in a speech delivered to a forum on risk capital in Munich on Friday.</p>
<p>In the text of the speech Waigel had said that the chance of reaching a compromise on this tax on January 1, 1998 were good. Waigel left out this paragraph when he delivered the speech.</p>
<p>-- Catherine O'Mahony, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
